    "body": "Okay, maybe it's parsing.\r\n\r\n```js\r\nconst d = document.createElement('div')\r\nd.innerHTML = `\r\n  <table>\r\n    <tr><div>foo</div><td></td></tr>\r\n  </table>\r\n`\r\nd.innerHTML\r\n```\r\n\r\noutput:\r\n\r\n```\r\n\"\r\n  <div>foo</div><table>\r\n    <tbody><tr><td></td></tr>\r\n  </tbody></table>\r\n\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nThat's much worse than what I'm doing with default attribute values.\r\n\r\nBut you're right, I can achieve this without setting an attribute value, but what problems would it cause if I do?",
